TI  - GMCRR_DPNet: A Gradient Multi-Level Convolutional and Residual Attention with a Regularized Weight Decay-Based Dengue Outbreak Prediction Network
PY  - 2026
AB  - This paper presents GMCRR_DPNet, a novel gradient multi-level Convolutional and Residual Attention network designed for predicting dengue outbreaks. The model integrates various data sources, including historical incidence rates, weather conditions, and demographic information, to enhance the accuracy of predictions. By employing advanced machine learning techniques, GMCRR_DPNet captures complex patterns and correlations that traditional methods may overlook. The architecture supports parallel processing of temporal and spatial features, allowing for a comprehensive understanding of the factors influencing dengue transmission. The incorporation of a self-adaptive metaheuristic algorithm (SA-BOA) enables real-time adjustments of model parameters, improving adaptability to changing environmental conditions. The paper addresses critical research gaps, such as the need for better data integration frameworks and the inclusion of diverse climatic variables, to enhance the generalizability of prediction models across different geographic contexts. The performance of GMCRR_DPNet is evaluated using key metrics, demonstrating its potential as a robust tool for public health management, facilitating timely interventions and effective resource allocation in response to dengue outbreaks.
