AB  - Dengue fever poses a significant and increasing global health threat, and factors such as climate change, rapid urbanization, inadequate public health infrastructure and epidemic outbreaks often burden health systems in areas of rainy and sunny and tropical areas. This review focuses on the application of advanced predictive analytics in health care, specifically AI-driven approaches to dengue outbreak detection and prevention. We explore and compare machine learning models including self-order mapping, decision trees, and support vector machines, while Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) and Correlation etc. We build performance using the best based patterns Feature focus selection (CFS). Combining soil variables, meteorological data, and real-time medical data, our approach provides a comprehensive and robust framework for dengue prediction These frameworks, if targeted, are helpful health authorities intervene, for better resource allocation and evidence-based policy delivery.
