TI  - Studying Dengue Spread using Climatic Conditions and Machine Learning Algorithms
PY  - 2024
AB  - Dengue is one of the serious mosquito-borne disease, which causes flu-like symptoms like high fever, sever headache, pain in joint, muscles, eyes etc. It is suggested to control mosquito populations in an area to avoid the disease. Our research aims on identifying climatic conditions which influence mosquito population to grow rapidly in an area, and find a machine learning algorithm that best predicts dengue risk in an area based on these climatic conditions. The dataset used was sourced from kaggle.com, in which after data cleaning we implemented algorithms like K-Nearest Neighbor, Logistic regression, Gaussian Naive Bayes and Random Forest on the cleaned dataset. Each algorithm was evaluated and compared on the basis of accuracy and confusion matrix out of which K-Nearest neighbor gave best results with 99.00% accuracy while offering superior performance in confusion matrix respectively, also Temperature, Humidity and Wind displayed best relation with spread of dengue diseases among other climatic conditions.
