AB  - This paper presented a novel dengue fever prediction method by combined local weather data and global El Nino-Southern Oscillation Index (ENSOI). There were six climatic data was collected: average minimum temperature, average maximum temperature, average dew point temperature in Hong Kong from 2004 to 2015. The relationship between dengue fever and climate data was analysed by Poisson regression model and a support vector machine (SVM). The results showed that climate factors significantly influence the incidence of dengue. where Poisson regression model illustrated that the SOI factor is overweight than others. Based on SVM method, the predication accuracy archived 78.5% when train data was from 2004-2013 and test data was from 2014-2015.
